WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:04.822
PostgreSQL FILTER attaches a condition directly to an aggregate.

00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:10.397
COUNT star FILTER where diagnosis equals Pneumonia counts only matching rows.

00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:17.382
The query is often easier to scan because the aggregate and its condition appear together.

00:00:17.382 --> 00:00:20.252
Run it and compare the result with the CASE version.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:26.247
The output should express the same business meaning.

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:33.787
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:35.762
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:43.972
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:43.972 --> 00:00:45.360
combination.
